{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792407189,"nonce":"I0IHkRKe3zyAWBsSO4H7Xo3bEYM=","message":"Notches are in f3746458666c2750421d16ec34ac0f9bd3591956 (local, not pushed). The ABI's signed corners become absolute radii and concave flags, and its two edge modifiers occupy the native notch slots. GpuPrimitive::notch_info carries the logical-to-device scale and fill/outer-shadow/inset-shadow mode, with zero retaining native shading. The struct is now 33 vec4 fields, 528 bytes; all twelve shader copies and the layout guards agree. SdfVertexInstance carries the metadata at vertex location 8.\n\nThe ABI's fixed logical join depths and shadow formulas have a separate binding-free helper in common/notch_abi.wgsl, composed alongside the existing prelude. Native notch shading stays on its previous path. The notch shaders also read gradient tables, conic fills and local clips. A notch border follows the producer's top width and top colour, including when the other sides differ. Layer translation now moves notch gradient geometry and conic centres. Notch rows on other record kinds remain explicitly unsupported.\n\nFixtures came from blinc_abi a92f5c0's encoder. Offscreen Apple M1 Pro, Metal: all 21 display-list tests and the polygon clip test pass. Twelve notch scenes cover mixed and compressed concave corners, top/bottom scoops, bulges, V cuts and peaks, translucent borders, a five-stop conic gradient, layer translation, outer and inset shadows, a general affine, and a turned local clip with fade. At display scales 1 and 2 every case is within 1/255 of an independent CPU oracle. The CPU shadow oracle integrates the normal density independently of the shader's erf approximation. Forcing the vertex-buffer path on the same adapter also passes every notch case within 1/255. Mutation: discarding the concave flags fails by 204/255. Comparing the native notch suite against the preceding shaders gives identical pixels.\n\nGate: fmt, workspace clippy, 1,880 workspace nextest tests (47 skipped), docs with warnings denied, wasm, iOS and threaded layout/CN tests pass. The separate DSL run again has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped, with exactly the same failing names as the untouched ff83adca baseline recorded under a33d2b9. No dependency or DSL sources changed. PowerVR/Adreno compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified; ce34b20 still tracks stale data-texture packing. Next: the clip-path frame, preserving the owner-coordination requirement before changing the shared ClipPath enum or CSS fill-rule keyword.","files":null}]}